# What the build stage is allowed to read.
#
# An allowlist, not a list of exclusions. A denylist fails silently in the
# expensive direction: a directory added to the repository later is copied into
# the build context by default, and nobody notices until the image is large or
# something private is inside it. Before this file existed the Dockerfile's
# `COPY . .` shipped .git, the built documentation site, node_modules and a
# local virtualenv into the image.
#
# The admitted set is exactly what building the wheel reads, which is the same
# set pyproject's sdist declares: the package, the skills it force-includes, and
# the three files hatchling opens (metadata, readme, licence).
*

!cpersona/
!skills/
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE

# Re-excluded after the directories above are admitted: compiled artifacts from
# a host interpreter are not inputs, and a stale one can shadow the source it
# was compiled from.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
